//! Surface-map simulator.
//!
//! Runs the live-translate pipeline against synthetic camera frames
//! warped from a reference image. The pipeline pieces — planar
//! tracker, PaddleOCR detection, recognition, surface map — are the
//! same as Android; only the camera-and-display layer is replaced
//! with "synth frame from a known reference" + "minifb window".
//!
//! The reference image is generated by rasterizing a small fixed
//! block of text into a high-resolution bitmap, so the sim is
//! self-contained and deterministic.
//!
//! Build and run:
//!     cargo run --release --features surface-sim --bin surface_sim
//!
//! Defaults look for models at
//! `/home/david/AndroidStudioProjects/bucket/ocr/1/PP-OCRv5/`;
//! override with `--model-dir <path>`.
//!
//! Window controls:
//!   Esc           quit
//!   Space         pause / resume
//!   N             next frame (when paused)
//!   R             reset pipeline (clear tracker + map)

